{
  "$schema_note": "Parser test fixtures (Rust). Each case's raw_input is parsed by the Rust parser. expected.ok asserts exact IR field values; the following expected.ok keys are OPTIONAL (asserted only when present, so pre-existing cases that omit them are unaffected): kiro_cli_tools_settings (KiroCliConfig.tools_settings, an arbitrary JSON object), kiro_cli_hooks (KiroCliConfig.hooks, a map of hook-name to array-of-{command}), kiro_cli_resources (KiroCliConfig.resources, exact ordered list), claude_cli_tools (ClaudeCliConfig.tools, exact ordered list), and dependencies.mcp_registry_entries (a map from mcp_registry_keys entries to their full {command, args, url} shape, for asserting an entry's fields beyond just its key presence). expected.error asserts the ParseError reason_substring (when set) and the error field: 'field' is the expectation the Rust loader reads, overridden by 'field_rust' when present; 'field_python' is a legacy key retained in the data from the removed Python consumer and is ignored by the Rust loader. A case may carry an optional '_source_note' field documenting which real agents/*.agent-spec.json file(s) its raw_input values were lifted from verbatim; this is documentation only and not read by either consumer. Consumed by cli/konductor-rs/src/cli/synth/parser.rs's fixture-driven test.",
